WEBVTT

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.610
We can get 16 pages per side.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.380
That's 32 pages in total
that get printed at a time.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.010
When this paper is folded in half
four times

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.080
they line up in sequence
both vertically and horizontally,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.520
meaning each sheet makes 16 pages.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.520
Excluding the spine of the book,

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.290
each pass is cut into threes.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:28.190
In other words, 32 pages with each pass.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.460
With Daitokai being around 3,000 pages

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.470
it will take over 90 passes
to make one book.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.140
We will work hard and do everything we can

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:42.610
in order to give shape
to your hard work and dedication.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.820
It's warm.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.260
"Akari."

00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:01.460
The word "akari" not only means light,

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.260
it can also mean "evidence."

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:09.240
Our long battle with words
was not a waste.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.340
This is clearly evidence of that.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.290
The Great Passage

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.090
A quiet dreamlike morning
The madder red sky

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.600
Shines through the window
And reflects on my pen

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:43.770
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.610
Deep thoughts, flexible conception

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.340
Foreseeable aspirations
Distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:56.780
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.220
The light in our eyes
That differ from each other

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.360
Traces of friendship
That’s not in the treaty

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:09.630
In the ocean that sweeps
The sand of eternity

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:16.700
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:23.180
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.740
Reference, conclusion

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.750
I’ll gather words that have
Scattered over many months and years

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.850
The fragrant sea breeze

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:36.160
The connection that rests on the seashore
Become one.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.940
Torch

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:57.410
When his wife answered and I told her
about Daitokai's advanced copies

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.380
the sensei rushed to the phone right away.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.950
He's doing well, then?

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.420
He sounded really happy.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.950
He said he couldn't wait
to hold one in his hands.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.740
MATSUMOTO

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:50.860
He's just taking a little rest.
I will go get him.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.470
Please, I don't want to disturb him.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:58.970
It's quite all right. If I sent the two of you
away now, I won't hear the end of it.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.410
Please, come in.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.640
- In that case...
- Pardon us.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.820
Oh, welcome!

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.650
Oh, please don't get up.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.490
- Could you get us some tea?
- Yes.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.390
It feels quite warm for winter today.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:27.400
Sensei, please have a look.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.440
We are still on schedule
to have it out by this spring.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.510
I cannot wait.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:37.680
But dictionary work only really starts
once it's completed.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.350
In order to increase its accuracy
and quality,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.680
you must still continue gathering words
after publication

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.690
and prepare for the revisions.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.960
It will forever be incomplete.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.430
I will take that to heart.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.010
Would you like to see our garden?

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.420
How are you, Majime?

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:20.390
The withered flora release their seeds

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:21.950
and sprout anew.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:29.030
There is nothing more encouraging to us
than the circle of life.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.870
The circle? The circle of life...

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:39.470
The sun is back out again.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.680
They have brought us some gifts.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:46.110
Thank you, this is quite something.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:50.350
I particularly love their Western snacks.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.720
He would always
buy more than we could eat

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:56.120
every time on his way home
from visiting Genbu Books Publishing.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:04.530
- I was wondering, Majime...
- Yes?

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.570
It's common overseas to have
their native-language dictionaries

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:12.410
edited under the guidance
of those in power.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:16.840
Why do you think they use public money
to compile a dictionary?

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:23.820
Perhaps the thinking is that
editing your native language's dictionary

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.950
is a matter of national pride?

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:27.390
Exactly.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:34.790
However, Japan has never produced
a dictionary by a public institution.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:40.470
Genkai was personally funded by
Fumihiko Otsuki's life savings.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.670
And he edited and published it himself.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:47.410
When I learned of that

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:53.050
I was appalled by the Japanese government's
complete lack of appreciation of culture.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:58.650
But now, I feel that it is okay
that it's been that way.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.890
Why is that?

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:08.060
When public funds are used,
they may want to interfere with its contents.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.960
The integrity of the words
cannot be compromised

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:14.070
by a desire for power or to use them
as a tool for control.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:21.070
Words and the hearts of those who use them
must remain free.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.680
Even with our scarce funding

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.980
we are individual people, not a nation.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:30.620
We spend our lives
editing the dictionaries.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:34.190
Let us take pride in this.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.590
That is what I believe now.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.660
- Sensei.
- He's okay.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:48.700
He likes to talk when he's in a good mood.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.610
It seems I got a little carried away.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:58.010
Sensei, we should be going now.
Please rest.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:05.180
Actually, there's something
I need to tell you.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:09.020
They found cancer in my esophagus.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.670
Can you believe this is happening?

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:27.270
- Well, Majime?
- No...

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:30.780
We will continue to make dictionaries.

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:34.510
Continue to build a ship
to navigate a sea of words.

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:40.620
- Yes.
- But where are we trying to head to, then?

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.860
I don't know

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.860
where we might be heading,

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:52.100
but when I first started
editing this dictionary

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:55.670
it was like discovering
a light inside the darkness for me.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:09:00.040
Like I finally found the direction
I should be heading in.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.310
But...

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:06.110
Even now, I sometimes have this dream.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:10.120
I am out in a dark ocean,
not knowing which direction to take.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.720
A dream of being lost.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:16.060
- Majime.
- But...

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:19.290
Now I know that I'm not the only one.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:24.030
Everyone is trying to
communicate their feelings.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.170
Being happy, being hurt...

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.870
Everyone putting everything on the line.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.710
What we can do

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:38.280
is to shine a light on those who try to
cross the ocean in the darkness.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:41.180
Even with small steps, we do not stop

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.180
so that we can one day
pass the baton to someone else.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:48.920
Would that be too sad to say?

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:55.030
No. I don't think it's sad at all!

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:56.860
You're right, Majime.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.700
To think the day would come
when you'd remind me of that.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.870
All right, you ready to do this?

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.870
Yes.

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.160
Are you ready to go?

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:22.070
- Now you're good.
- Thank you.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.880
- Look!
- They're budding.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:35.950
Why don't we go flower gazing
when you get some downtime from work?

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.190
We can take some tea and sandwiches.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:43.220
We'll walk, take a break when we're tired,
and then walk again.

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:47.260
Let's really take our time.

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:49.100
That sounds nice.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.410
Daddy!

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.340
Hurry up!

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:07.310
All right, my princesses,
are you ready to go?

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:09.950
I thought I was your princess too.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.090
Mama, you're the queen!

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:17.860
Only the princesses get to be carried.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:21.330
Unfortunately, if I have to
carry the queen as well

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:25.470
your king will be flattened
like a pancake!

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.100
What? What do you mean by that?!

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:32.470
Oh, no! Let's get out of here, girls!

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.840
Genbu Books Publishing

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:37.440
Thank you for your call.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.980
- Yes.
- Good morning.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.480
I understand.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:45.050
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:48.490
- Good morning.
- Have a nice day.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:52.330
The printer just said
that they've finished the last printing.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.760
It's almost here.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.360
I'm just filled with emotion.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:02.000
When Daitokai is finally finished,
I think I might just cry.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:06.210
- I can't imagine you crying.
- That's mean.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:09.040
Yes, that was very mean, Araki-san.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:12.010
You're right, I'm sorry.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.410
Yes?

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.380
This is Genbu Books Publishing's
Dictionary Editorial Department.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:20.520
Oh, yes. It was good to see you again.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:23.060
Thank you very much.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.580
I've just heard

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:43.510
that Mastumoto-sensei...

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.510
Matsumoto-sensei

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:51.920
had passed away.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.420
To Nishioka:
Matsumoto-sensei has passed away.

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:01.360
Vice chief! The meeting is about to start.

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:04.400
- Vice chief?
- Nishioka-san?

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:12.070
Daitokai is our new dictionary
that will bring about a new age this spring.

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:15.040
With the final hour approaching,

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:18.980
I'd like to touch bases
and confirm what all our roles will be.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.180
But before that

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:25.890
you may not believe me

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:31.090
despite my appearances,
I used to be in the dictionary-editing game.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.460
And there's something I learned
during that time.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:38.270
Dictionaries are tools to help people
understand one another

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:42.440
and create a better society for the world.

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:45.340
Daitokai was born from the desire

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:53.280
for it to be a guiding light
for the present and the future.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:56.120
Our task is to ensure
that this new dictionary

00:13:56.250 --> 00:14:00.890
can find its way
to as many readers as possible.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.460
I couldn't be more proud.

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:16.040
Micchan, food's ready.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:34.590
Nights are still chilly.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.710
I couldn't make it in time.

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:21.130
Chief Majime. Congratulations on
the publication of Daitokai.

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.640
It has been a long road, Majime-san.

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:26.570
Thank you for all of your hard work.

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:30.340
This still doesn't feel real to me.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.580
I don't know what to say.

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:34.310
I'm just the same!

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:38.590
- You too, Sasaki-san?
- You too, Araki-san?

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.690
Me too.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:45.760
Let's all go out and celebrate!
For Matsumoto-sensei too.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.430
I've already made a reservation
at Tsuki no Ura.

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.430
We've also invited Nishioka.

00:15:50.560 --> 00:15:56.070
Nishioka, huh? Who else would
come up with that mascot, right?

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.640
He's so cute.

00:15:57.770 --> 00:16:00.110
Apparently he's popular
at the book stores too.

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:02.780
I suppose I can tell him
he's done a good job.

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:06.410
- Shall we go then?
- Yes!

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:12.020
I'd like to organize some things here
before I go.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:16.260
- I can do the organizing for you.
- I think he means his thoughts.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:20.360
I'm sorry. I'll be right there.

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.610
- Yo.
- Nishioka-san?

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:43.120
So my name is listed at
the end of Daitokai?

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:46.090
Yes... Oh, no.

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:48.190
Was your name misspelled?!

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:53.160
No, it's not that.
It's that I didn't really do much.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:58.670
Honestly, you are just...

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:05.440
Do you remember talking about the entry
for Saigyo with me here?

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:06.610
I do.

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:10.210
I remember what Matsumoto-sensei said
to us then.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.850
That we respected our strengths
and complemented each other.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:15.220
Yes.

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:19.450
I think I better understand
what he meant now.

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.660
It's not just us.

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:26.860
People have to support each other
in order to make it across the ocean.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.860
I feel the same way. And...

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:34.630
Daitokai can help in that.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:41.710
- Great work. Congratulations on finishing.
- You too, Nishioka-san.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:44.640
But don't think you're finished.

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.350
My work has just begun.

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:52.590
I know. Our work will never be finished.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:54.220
What? Never?

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:56.520
Please, you gotta give me a break here.

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:57.860
Why is that?

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:02.360
You're starting to become
just like Matsumoto-sensei.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:06.170
- You too, Nishioka-san.
- Me? No way.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:07.600
Really?

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:12.270
Shall we go then?
Everyone's waiting for us.

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:15.340
All right, I guess we can go.

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:41.870
Genbu Books Publishing
Daitokai Launch Party

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:50.610
Hey

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:58.350
It’s a full moon tonight

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:01.820
I speak to you

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:09.260
Softly as you sleep

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:13.500
Your gestures

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:16.340
Attitude

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:21.370
And way of life

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:28.210
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:19:28.380 --> 00:19:33.920
So please stay the way you are

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:39.860
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:45.430
Here with you, forever by your side

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.340
I’ve loved you

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:53.440
From the day

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:58.610
We met

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:07.550
I apologize to everyone
on the Editorial team

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:11.460
that I was unable to see this through
to the very end.

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:17.400
I will most likely no longer be here
when Daitokai is finally finished.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:21.800
-But I have neither worry or regret...
-Worry or regret.

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:28.010
That is because I can vividly see
our Daitokai

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:30.380
crossing the great sea of words.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:34.350
Araki, there is one thing I'd like to amend.

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:40.350
I once told you that I would never meet
another editor like you.

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:42.590
But I was mistaken.

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:45.890
Thanks to you bringing Majime aboard

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:51.430
I was able to push forward on this path
of dictionaries once again.

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:54.370
I am truly glad

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.500
to have met editors like you and Majime.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:03.810
Thanks to you, I was able to live
a truly fulfilling and accomplished life.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:07.550
If there is an afterlife,
I plan to continue collecting my words

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:12.620
and see if there is a word
that goes beyond gratitude.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:18.860
How fun it has been editing Daitokai.

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:26.770
I pray for a long and happy voyage
to all of you and Daitokai.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:36.840
Sometimes I imagine
that we are all travelers

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:43.720
and dictionaries are guiding lights
to show us travelers the way.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:46.850
As long as people continue to travel

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:51.460
they will be inherited,
repeatedly rewritten,

00:21:51.590 --> 00:21:54.490
and continue to show travelers the way.

00:21:55.030 --> 00:21:57.100
That is what I believe.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.430
And we will build another ship once again.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.800
Light: A small fire or light. Torch.
A light shows us the way.
